Secure Multi-VLAN Infrastructure

Overview

This project focused on the design, deployment, and validation of a secure enterprise-style multi-VLAN network infrastructure. The environment was built within a virtualized lab and included network segmentation, centralized authentication, infrastructure services, web applications, and security controls.

The goal was to simulate a real-world network architecture while implementing best practices for routing, firewalling, service management, and access control.

---

Project Goals

- Design a routed multi-VLAN environment
- Implement network segmentation using VLANs
- Configure inter-VLAN routing
- Deploy DNS and DHCP services
- Implement Active Directory Domain Services
- Configure firewall policies and access restrictions
- Deploy internal and externally accessible services
- Validate network functionality through testing and packet analysis

---

