Restricted Target

- Metasploitable 3 (Windows)

---

Security Features

Network Segmentation

Services were separated into dedicated VLANs to reduce the attack surface and limit unnecessary communication between systems.

Firewall Controls

Firewall rules were implemented to:

- Allow Internet access to public-facing services
- Restrict Internet access to sensitive systems
- Control communication between VLANs
- Enforce access restrictions based on business requirements

Centralized Authentication

Windows Active Directory was configured to provide:

- Domain-based authentication
- Centralized user management
- Kerberos authentication
- LDAP directory services

DNS-Based Access

All services were configured to be accessed through Fully Qualified Domain Names (FQDNs) rather than direct IP addresses.

